{
  "report_markdown": "# Cap Table \u2014 Acmecorp\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nModeled 2 scenario(s) for Acmecorp: 1 full, 0 mixed, 0 repay-only, 1 pending input.\n16 counsel-review item(s) surfaced. 14 date-sensitive item(s) in watchlist.\nFounder ownership ranges 47.5% to 47.5% across resolved scenarios.\n\n> \u26a0 **Cap base was NOT produced by the deterministic spreadsheet mapper.** It was entered\n> manually or extracted from a document (PDF / Carta / pasted), so it was not\n> mechanically verified against a structured source. Confirm each holder/class against the\n> source before relying on these numbers.\n\n## Current Cap State\n\nAs of: 2026-08-01\n\n| Holder | Shares (as-converted) | % of FD |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Alex Stone | 4,000,000 | 44.4% |\n| Sam Lee | 3,500,000 | 38.9% |\n| Options outstanding | 500,000 | 5.6% |\n| Options available | 1,000,000 | 11.1% |\n| **Total fully-diluted** | **9,000,000** | **100.0%** |\n\nOutstanding SAFEs: 1\n\n## Scenarios Modeled\n\n### Series A + SAFE conversion + TargetCo acquisition (Priced round)\n\n**Stage:** Fully modeled (`full`)\n\n**Inputs:**\n- `pre_money`: 16000000\n- `new_money`: 4000000\n- `acquisition`: {'acquired_entity': 'TargetCo Ltd', 'consideration_pct': 0.2, 'consideration_form': 'shares', 'acquisition_timing': 'concurrent_with_round'}\n\n**Post-round ownership:**\n- founders pct: 47.5%\n- preferred pct: 0.0%\n- option pool pct: 9.5%\n- safe pct: 3.0%\n- note pct: 0.0%\n- new money pct: 20.0%\n- acquisition pct: 20.0%\n\n**Equity financing price:** $1.2667/share\n\n**Founder Impact Lens:** Founders collectively held 83.3% of fully-diluted shares before this scenario; after, 47.5%. That's -35.8 percentage points.\n\n**Per-SAFE conversion math:**\n\n| SAFE | Branch | Purchase \u00f7 Cap | Conversion price | Conversion shares |\n|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n| `safe_foobar` | `cap_branch` | \u2014 | $1.0556 | 473,684 |\n\n_Provenance: rules: `acquisition.consideration_shares`, `safe.post_money_cap_conversion`_\n\n### Israeli \u2192 Delaware flip (Entity flip)\n\n**Stage:** Structure only \u2014 no priced round yet (`structural_only`)\n\n**Inputs:**\n- `iia_grants_in_history`: False\n- `section_102_grants_outstanding`: 500000\n\n_Provenance: rules: `delaware_flip.share_exchange_mechanics`_\n\n## Scenario Comparison\n\n| Scenario | Stage | Founder %  | Equity Price |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Series A + SAFE conversion + TargetCo acquisition | Fully modeled | 47.5% | $1.2667 |\n| Israeli \u2192 Delaware flip | Structure only \u2014 no priced round yet | \u2014 | \u2014 |\n\n## Counsel Review Required\n\n### Acquisition\n- **[Negotiated-% acquisition consideration shares](https://www.ycombinator.com/assets/ycdc/Primer%20for%20post-money%20safe%20v1.1-2af8129e12effd9638eeab383b7309142c8f415e5cdb0bc210d573f779177a1c.pdf)** (`acquisition.consideration_shares`)\n  - An acquired entity's holders receive consideration shares C equal to a negotiated percentage t of post-close fully-diluted; C = t * post_FD, solved inside the priced round via D = numerator/(1 - t*k), k = 1 + new_money/pre_money.\n- **Post-money pool denominator includes acquisition consideration** (`acquisition.pool_consideration_basis`)\n  - When the option pool target is post-money fully-diluted and an acquisition closes in connection with the round, the consideration shares C are part of the post-close denominator the pool is sized against (default include); excluding C is a negotiable term.\n- **[Acquisition timing drives SAFE Company-Capitalization inclusion](https://www.ycombinator.com/assets/ycdc/Primer%20for%20post-money%20safe%20v1.1-2af8129e12effd9638eeab383b7309142c8f415e5cdb0bc210d573f779177a1c.pdf)** (`acquisition.timing`)\n  - A concurrent acquisition's consideration is excluded from the YC post-money SAFE Company Capitalization (so it dilutes the SAFE via post_fd only); a pre-round-closed acquisition is stock outstanding immediately prior (folded into Company Capitalization, protecting the SAFE).\n\n### Delaware Cross Border\n- **[Delaware parent with Israeli subsidiary is a common cross-border structure](https://kpmg.com/us/en/taxnewsflash/news/2025/11/israel-final-guidance-local-r-and-d-centers-ip-valuations.html)** \u00b7 [The Tax Adviser](https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2025/dec/revisiting-sec-1202-strategic-planning-after-the-2025-obbba-expansion/) (`delaware_cross_border.structure_note`)\n  - A Delaware parent with an Israeli operating or R&D subsidiary is common for US venture-backed Israeli-linked startups, but structure choice is tax, IP, investor, and employment dependent.\n- **[Cross-border IP ownership and transfer pricing](https://kpmg.com/us/en/taxnewsflash/news/2025/11/israel-final-guidance-local-r-and-d-centers-ip-valuations.html)** (`delaware_cross_border.ip_transfer_pricing`)\n  - Does flip require IP migration, and what's the \u00a785A / OECD transfer-pricing exposure?\n- **[\u00a7102 continuity for 500000 outstanding grants](https://www.icnl.org/wp-content/uploads/Israel_Ordinance.pdf)** \u00b7 [Pearl Cohen](https://www.pearlcohen.com/section-102-options-the-unwritten-rules-and-pitfalls-to-look-for/) (`delaware_cross_border.section_102_parent_shares`)\n  - What sub-plan and trustee arrangements continue \u00a7102 treatment under foreign-parent shares?\n\n### Delaware Flip\n- **[Flip mechanics require holder-by-holder mapping](https://arnontl.com/news/significant-tax-reliefs-in-corporate-restructuring-amendment-to-the-israeli-income-tax-ordinance/)** \u00b7 [International Center for Not-for-Profit Law library](https://www.icnl.org/wp-content/uploads/Israel_Ordinance.pdf) (`delaware_flip.share_exchange_mechanics`)\n  - What share-exchange / contribution structure preserves economic rights and minimizes tax friction?\n- **[\u00a7104H / \u00a7103K / \u00a785A tax-deferral route choice](https://kpmg.com/us/en/taxnewsflash/news/2025/11/israel-final-guidance-local-r-and-d-centers-ip-valuations.html)** \u00b7 [The Tax Adviser](https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2025/dec/revisiting-sec-1202-strategic-planning-after-the-2025-obbba-expansion/) (`delaware_flip.tax_route_decision`)\n  - Which tax route applies to this flip (104H reorganization, 103K asset transfer, 85A IP migration)?\n\n### Israel Equity Tax\n- **[Section 102 capital-gains track checklist](https://www.icnl.org/wp-content/uploads/Israel_Ordinance.pdf)** \u00b7 [Pearl Cohen](https://www.pearlcohen.com/section-102-options-the-unwritten-rules-and-pitfalls-to-look-for/) (`israel_equity_tax.section_102_capital_gains`)\n  - Israeli Section 102 capital-gains treatment depends on trustee deposit, timing, employee status, approved plan mechanics, and holding-period requirements; secondary guidance should be used only as a checklist.\n- **[Section 102 plan-design pitfalls](https://www.pearlcohen.com/section-102-options-the-unwritten-rules-and-pitfalls-to-look-for/)** (`israel_equity_tax.section_102_plan_design`)\n  - Plan terms such as share class, voting rights, cash settlement, exit-only rights, repurchase arrangements, and transaction-adjacent grants can affect Israeli tax analysis. Section 102 trustee track is administratively limited to ordinary voting shares; preferred or non-voting shares typically require an ITA pre-ruling.\n- **[Section 102 double-trigger acceleration treatment](https://www.shibolet.com/en/double-trigger-acceleration-upon-exit-or-ipo/)** \u00b7 [Pearl Cohen](https://www.pearlcohen.com/section-102-options-the-unwritten-rules-and-pitfalls-to-look-for/) (`israel_equity_tax.section_102_double_trigger`)\n  - Israeli law-firm guidance reports that under ITA Position Paper 01/2025, double-trigger acceleration of Section 102 awards on exit or IPO is not treated as a violation of Section 102. The resulting tax characterization on exit still depends on facts (cash vs equity consideration, post-closing share price movement).\n- **[Section 3(i) nonemployee equity](https://www.icnl.org/wp-content/uploads/Israel_Ordinance.pdf)** \u00b7 [Pearl Cohen](https://www.pearlcohen.com/section-102-options-the-unwritten-rules-and-pitfalls-to-look-for/) (`israel_equity_tax.section_3i_nonemployee`)\n  - Israeli equity or option grants to consultants, service providers, controlling shareholders, or other non-Section 102 recipients may fall outside Section 102 and require separate tax treatment.\n\n### Israeli Ltd\n- **[Israeli private company share register](https://www.icnl.org/wp-content/uploads/Israel_CompaniesLaw.pdf)** (`israeli_ltd.share_register`)\n  - An Israeli private company must maintain a shareholder register and the cap-table model should separate internal share-register truth from reportable filings.\n- **[Israeli Registrar online reporting](https://barlaw.co.il/practice_areas/corporate/client_updates/compulsory-online-reporting-to-the-israeli-registrar-of-companies/)** (`israeli_ltd.registrar_online_reporting`)\n  - Law-firm guidance reports that from June 27, 2024, most filings with the Israeli Registrar of Companies must be submitted online; the cap-table skill should flag filing workflow rather than attempt filings.\n\n### Safe\n- **[Israel 2025 SAFE temporary guidance](https://www.gov.il/BlobFolder/policy/procedures-290125/he/IncomeTax_procedures-290125.pdf)** \u00b7 [Herzog Law](https://herzoglaw.co.il/en/news-and-insights/the-ita-publishes-an-updated-version-of-its-guidance-and-safe-harbor-for-safes/) \u00b7 [Pearl Cohen](https://www.pearlcohen.com/key-tax-updates-safe-2025-summary-key-changes-from-safe-2023/) (`safe.israeli_2025_safe_harbor`)\n  - The January 2025 ITA SAFE circular (gov.il primary, corroborated by Herzog and Pearl Cohen) applies to qualifying Israeli-company SAFEs signed during 2025-2026 and uses quantitative conditions such as investment caps, ownership limits, minimum discounts, and conversion timing constraints.\n- **[Non-qualifying Israeli SAFE facts-and-circumstances review](https://www.gov.il/BlobFolder/policy/procedures-290125/he/IncomeTax_procedures-290125.pdf)** \u00b7 [Herzog Law](https://herzoglaw.co.il/en/news-and-insights/the-ita-publishes-an-updated-version-of-its-guidance-and-safe-harbor-for-safes/) \u00b7 [Pearl Cohen](https://www.pearlcohen.com/key-tax-updates-safe-2025-summary-key-changes-from-safe-2023/) (`safe.israeli_safe_facts_circumstances`)\n  - If a SAFE does not satisfy the January 2025 ITA SAFE circular's conditions (gov.il primary), the instrument remains facts-and-circumstances dependent and may be treated as debt, equity, or another instrument for tax purposes.\n\n## Source Notes\n\n_Informational citations for cap-table conventions applied above. Each note is tied to a rule in the rule pack with its primary-source citations._\n\n### Delaware Cross Border\n- **[Delaware parent with Israeli subsidiary is a common cross-border structure](https://kpmg.com/us/en/taxnewsflash/news/2025/11/israel-final-guidance-local-r-and-d-centers-ip-valuations.html)** \u00b7 [The Tax Adviser](https://www.thetaxadviser.com/issues/2025/dec/revisiting-sec-1202-strategic-planning-after-the-2025-obbba-expansion/) (`delaware_cross_border.structure_note`)\n  - A Delaware parent with an Israeli operating or R&D subsidiary is common for US venture-backed Israeli-linked startups, but structure choice is tax, IP, investor, and employment dependent.\n\n## Date-Sensitive Watchlist\n\n_7 rule(s) to watch (from 7 matched instances)._\n\n| Rule | Status | When | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Israel 2025 SAFE temporary guidance](https://www.gov.il/BlobFolder/policy/procedures-290125/he/IncomeTax_procedures-290125.pdf) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the safe investment date for this instance. |\n| [Israeli Registrar online reporting](https://barlaw.co.il/practice_areas/corporate/client_updates/compulsory-online-reporting-to-the-israeli-registrar-of-companies/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the filing date for this instance. |\n| [Non-qualifying Israeli SAFE facts-and-circumstances review](https://www.gov.il/BlobFolder/policy/procedures-290125/he/IncomeTax_procedures-290125.pdf) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the safe investment date for this instance. |\n| [Section 102 capital-gains track checklist](https://www.icnl.org/wp-content/uploads/Israel_Ordinance.pdf) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the grant date for this instance. |\n| [Section 102 double-trigger acceleration treatment](https://www.shibolet.com/en/double-trigger-acceleration-upon-exit-or-ipo/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the transaction event date for this instance. |\n| [Section 102 plan-design pitfalls](https://www.pearlcohen.com/section-102-options-the-unwritten-rules-and-pitfalls-to-look-for/) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the grant date for this instance. |\n| [Section 3(i) nonemployee equity](https://www.icnl.org/wp-content/uploads/Israel_Ordinance.pdf) | Needs a date from you | \u2014 | Provide the grant date for this instance. |\n\n### For-Reference Annotations\n\n_7 item(s) \u2014 rules that don't apply to this engagement in its current state (different jurisdiction, no grants, etc.) but are tracked in case the engagement evolves. No action needed today._\n\n## Sources Cited\n\n- `ARNONTL-RESTRUCTURING-2025`\n- `BARNEA-REGISTRAR-ONLINE`\n- `COOLEY-PRICING-METHODS`\n- `ICNL-ISRAEL-ORDINANCE`\n- `ISRAEL-COMPANIES-LAW`\n- `ITA-SAFE-2025-HERZOG`\n- `ITA-SAFE-2025-PRIMARY`\n- `KPMG-RD-CENTER-2025`\n- `PEARLCOHEN-102-PITFALLS`\n- `PEARLCOHEN-SAFE-2025`\n- `SHIBOLET-102-DOUBLE-TRIGGER`\n- `TAXADVISER-QSBS-OBBBA`\n- `YC-PMSAFE-PRIMER`\n- `YC-SAFE-DOCUMENTS`\n\n---\n\n<!-- COACHING_INSERTION_POINT_a6cb62b1 -->\n\n---\n\n*Generated by [founder skills](https://github.com/lool-ventures/founder-skills) by [lool ventures](https://lool.vc) \u2014 Cap Table Agent \u00b7 [Share feedback](https://github.com/lool-ventures/founder-skills/discussions/new?category=ideas-feedback)*\n",
